        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0192" n="80" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg80"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811B.5034.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Belgian
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to transmit herewith, for your
                    information, a copy of an opinion rendered by the Attorney General, dated April
                    29, 1910, upon the question presented by Mr. Ed. C. André, through you, as to
                    the legal right of a Belgian corporation to purchase and hold a plantation in
                    the Philippine Islands containing an area of 1,430 hectares. As will be
                    observed, the Attorney General holds that under the law no foreign or domestic
                    corporation authorized to engage in agriculture may purchase or hold lands in
                    the Philippines in excess of 1,024 hectares.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d54-a1.xml" xpointer="d54-a1"/>
